WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.660
Containment limits the spread or impact of an incident while the team continues to understand and resolve it.

2
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.490
Containment can be narrow or broad depending on risk and confidence.

3
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:19.449
Conceptually, it may involve isolating affected systems, disabling accounts, restricting access, blocking traffic, pausing a workflow,

4
00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:22.152
rotating credentials, or applying temporary controls.

5
00:00:22.302 --> 00:00:26.983
The important point is that containment is a decision with tradeoffs.

6
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:30.537
Acting too slowly can allow harm to grow.

7
00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:37.070
Acting too broadly can disrupt operations, interrupt customers, or remove evidence that analysts still need.

8
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:45.305
Good containment is therefore coordinated with incident leadership, system owners, business owners, and legal or privacy stakeholders when appropriate.

9
00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:52.689
Responders should ask what the action protects, what it might break, what evidence must be preserved first,

10
00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:57.095
and how the action will be reversed or adjusted later.

11
00:00:57.245 --> 00:01:01.500
Temporary controls can buy time for deeper analysis and eradication.

12
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:08.459
Every containment decision should leave a record: what was done, who approved it, when it happened,

13
00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:12.013
what risk it addressed, and what follow-up remains.

14
00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:17.269
Containment plans should include both the immediate action and the exit path.

15
00:01:17.419 --> 00:01:21.674
If an account is disabled, how will legitimate work continue?

16
00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:26.080
If a host is isolated, who validates it can return?

17
00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:30.911
If traffic is blocked, what monitoring confirms the block is helping?

18
00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:34.890
These questions make containment safer and easier to explain.
